---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "Noise Phobia and Anxiety Training San Jacinto | Good Doggos";
const description = "Help your dog survive storms, fireworks, and sirens in San Jacinto. We build resilience and confidence against noise phobia using a balanced 'bridge of certainty'.";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "Noise Phobia and Sensitivity Training",
  "description": description,
  "provider": {
    "@type": "LocalBusiness",
    "name": "Good Doggos",
    "url": "https://gooddoggos.com",
    "telephone": "+19514016252",
    "address": {
      "@type": "PostalAddress",
      "addressLocality": "San Jacinto",
      "addressRegion": "CA",
      "addressCountry": "US"
    }
  },
  "areaServed": {
    "@type": "AdministrativeArea",
    "name": "Riverside County"
  },
  "url": "https://gooddoggos.com/services/noise-phobia-training"
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
  </Fragment>

  <!-- Hero Band -->
  <section class="bg-primary-navy pt-32 pb-16 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <!-- Breadcrumb -->
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-body text-white/50 mt-6 mb-4" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/" class="text-accent-gold hover:text-accent-gold/80 underline font-semibold">Home</a>
        <span>&rsaquo;</span>
        <a href="/services/pet-trainer" class="text-accent-gold hover:text-accent-gold/80 underline font-semibold">Pet Trainer</a>
        <span>&rsaquo;</span>
        <span class="text-white/80 truncate">Noise Phobia Training</span>
      </nav>

      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-heading font-bold text-white leading-tight mb-6">
        Noise Phobia and Sensitivity Training in San Jacinto
      </h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Body Content -->
  <section class="py-16 px-4 bg-[#FCF9FA]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-12">
      
      <!-- Main Content -->
      <div class="prose max-w-none">
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          If you’ve spent the Fourth of July in a bathtub with a shaking dog or watched your pet bolt at a summer thunderstorm in the San Jacinto Valley, you know the feeling of helplessness.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          Noise phobia is a visceral meltdown. These extreme reactions are symptoms of a dog living in a state of constant fear. Because we are professionals, we do not guess or hand out generic advice. We must evaluate your dog in person to find the "bridge of certainty" they need to build resilience through a balanced approach.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-primary-navy mt-12 mb-6">
          Desensitization with a Balanced Backbone
        </h2>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          At Good Doggos, I don't believe in letting a dog suffer. For 8 years, I’ve worked with the most extreme noise-sensitive dogs in Riverside County. My approach focuses on building a "bridge of certainty." I use systematic desensitization, pairing sounds with rewards, but I also provide a physical "anchor" using "Balanced Clarity."
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          I remember a dog that would go into a blind panic every time a jet flew over from March ARB. By using calibrated leash work to provide structure, we prevented the "bolt" reflex and gave the dog a sense of safety. I paired the sound of the jets with high-value play and a calm, firm leadership state. Now, the dog just looks to the owner for direction when the jets fly over. They aren't "fixed"—they are confident and resilient.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          We don't train with a soundboard in a closet; we work at Hiram Deville Park and near State Street to show your dog how to "reset" after a startle. I’ll teach you how to be a calm leader who doesn't feed into the panic by coddling. Your dog’s mindset will shift from "the world is ending" to "that was just a noise, and my human has it under control."
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6 font-bold">
          Build your dog's confidence today. Apply for a Free Behavioral Assessment.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════
     CTA BAND
══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="relative overflow-hidden bg-[#FBF1E9]" style="border-top: 1px solid #E6DAC6;">
  <div class="w-full h-[3px]" style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #0F6D72, #D1B27F, #0F6D72);"></div>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-20 md:py-24 text-center">
    <p class="text-[11px] font-bold tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-4" style="color: rgba(15,109,114,0.60);">Your Dog Is Next</p>
    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-4" style="color: #0B2744;">
      Ready to See What's Possible?<br/>
      <span class="headline-accent" style="color: #D1B27F; font-style: italic; font-weight: 700;">Start With a Free Assessment.</span>
    </h2>
    <p class="text-base mb-10 max-w-lg mx-auto" style="color: rgba(17,32,50,0.60);">
      Tell us about your dog. We'll do an honest assessment and point you toward the right program — or tell you if we're not the right fit.
    </p>
    <a href="/apply"
       class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 font-bold text-sm tracking-widest uppercase rounded-full transition-all duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5"
       style="background: #D1B27F; color: #0B2744; padding: 18px 44px; box-shadow: 0 6px 24px rgba(209,178,127,0.35);">
      Apply for Free Behavioral Assessment →
    </a>
    <p class="mt-4 text-xs" style="color: rgba(17,32,50,0.40);">Takes less than 3 minutes · No commitment required</p>
  </div>
</div>
</Layout>
